        "v": 5,
        "title": "Prompt caching refactor and file request limits",
        "summary": "Prompt caching implementation (#96) refactors system prompt structure in `agent-system-prompt.ts` to use explicit `cache_control` blocks, removing dynamic file history injection from the base prompt. `check-new-files-necessary.ts` and `request-files-prompt.ts` remove `previousFiles` dependency, relying on conversation history for context, while capping file requests at 30 (`MAX_FILES_PER_REQUEST`). `main-prompt.ts` updates tool result handling to support simplified read-file results and partitioning logic.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T16:26:54.174Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The assistant no longer carries a running list of previously read files into every new question it considers; instead, it relies solely on the conversation history to decide whether more files are needed, and it will not request more than 30 files at once. A reusable snippet of instructions has been replaced by a single, explicitly marked copy that the system can reuse, making the assistant faster and cheaper to query. This is live today for anyone using the backend service.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
        "src": "bd973a19a1ec",
        "at": "2026-09-17T21:17:41.987Z"
      },
